me":"Thomsen, Jacob Bay","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolaj","key":"valstednicolajpau","last":"Valsted","name":"Valsted, Nicolaj","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vestergaardannapau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Anna","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christoffer","key":"karoffchristofferpau","last":"Karoff","locid":"b71daf07-cedf-42bb-bd7c-b0af441e57cd","name":"Karoff, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0003-2009-7965","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/frsen.2024.1474560","issn":["26736187"],"journal":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","paperid":"1474560","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208798743"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ca4b833d-fa44-4572-9b87-8dda8c791fee","sdu-c53e86ae-0f83-4d4c-b84c-dc476842298f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"DISCO-2 – an ambitious earth observing student CubeSat for arctic climate research","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-767862","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Capacitive micromachined ultrasonic transducers (CMUTs) have a nonlinear relationship between the applied voltage and the emitted signal, which is detrimental to conventional contrast enhanced ultrasound (CEUS) techniques. Instead, a three-pulse amplitude modulation (AM) sequence has been proposed, which is not adversely affected by the nonlinearly emitted harmonics. In this paper, this is shown theoretically, and the performance of the sequence is verified using a 4.8 MHz linear capacitive micromachined ultrasonic transducer (CMUT) array, and a comparable lead zirconate titanate (PZT) array, across 6–60 V applied alternating current (AC) voltage. CEUS images of the contrast agent SonoVue flowing through a 3D printed hydrogel phantom showed an average enhancement in contrast-to-tissue ratio (CTR) between B-mode and CEUS images of 49.9 and 37.4 dB for the PZT array and CMUT, respectively. Furthermore, hydrophone recordings of the emitted signals showed that the nonlinear emissions from the CMUT did not significantly degrade the cancellation in the compounded AM signal, leaving an average of 2% of the emitted power between 26 and 60 V of AC. Thus, it is demonstrated that CMUTs are capable of CEUS imaging independent of the applied excitation voltage when using a three-pulse AM sequence.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Ommen, Martin Lind","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","Diederichsen, Søren Elmin","Thomsen, Erik Vilain","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Larsen, Niels Bent","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331244"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Øygard, Sigrid Husebø"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contrast enhanced ultrasound imaging using capacitive micromachined ultrasonic transducers","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/314465379/1887_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331244","identifier":[{"id":"85151050557","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37002075","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-59b2aa2f-062f-48dc-9d0c-467305623cd4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E41EC03C969CEA3956DFABF82150A70D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/314465379/1887_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/340295726/Article.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, UltraSound and Biomechanics, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigrid Husebø","key":"øygardpau","last":"Øygard","locid":"91316990-5af9-4a30-8cfc-d293dc4bd2e5","name":"Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","orcid":"0000-0002-3021-7812","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Lind","key":"ommenpau","last":"Ommen","locid":"e7aebb26-b70d-4857-8c80-0040af9b6102","name":"Ommen, Martin Lind","orcid":"0000-0001-9206-6426","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Borislav Gueorguiev","key":"tomovpau","last":"Tomov","locid":"16c6d791-3a1a-47ad-a725-2da30c420dee","name":"Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","orcid":"0000-0003-4236-3056","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Elmin","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"bba32c4b-928b-44b9-9394-d0367a361ee6","name":"Diederichsen, Søren Elmin","orcid":"0000-0003-0686-913X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Vilain","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"822fe159-0932-4e5e-aeb6-b8b7f8421ab0","name":"Thomsen, Erik Vilain","orcid":"0000-0002-2772-926X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bent","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a727b09-e209-47ab-80f7-9df731c2178f","name":"Larsen, Niels Bent","orcid":"0000-0001-6506-3991","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37002075"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1121/10.0017533","issn":["00014966","01630962"],"issn_org":["00014966"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","pages":"1887-1897","publisher":"Acoustical Society of America","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Acoustical Society of America","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151050557"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-59b2aa2f-062f-48dc-9d0c-467305623cd4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Contrast-enhanced ultrasound imaging using capacitive micromachined ultrasonic transducers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-331244","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Barents Sea is one of the Polar regions where current climate and ecosystem change is most pronounced. Here we review the current state of knowledge of the physical, chemical and biological systems in the Barents Sea. Physical conditions in this area are characterized by large seasonal contrasts between partial sea-ice cover in winter and spring versus predominantly open water in summer and autumn. Observations over recent decades show that surface air and ocean temperatures have increased, sea-ice extent has decreased, ocean stratification has weakened, and water chemistry and ecosystem components have changed, the latter in a direction often described as “Atlantification” or “borealisation,” with a less “Arctic” appearance. Temporal and spatial changes in the Barents Sea have a wider relevance, both in the context of large-scale climatic (air, water mass and sea-ice) transport processes and in comparison to other Arctic regions. These observed changes also have socioeconomic consequences, including for fisheries and other human activities. While several of the ongoing changes are monitored and quantified, observation and knowledge gaps remain, especially for winter months when field observations and sample collections are still sparse. Knowledge of the interplay of physical and biogeochemical drivers and ecosystem responses, including complex feedback processes, needs further development.","author_count":41,"contributors":["Gerland, Sebastian","Ingvaldsen, Randi B.","Reigstad, Marit","Sundfjord, Arild","Bogstad, Bjarte","Chierici, Melissa","Hop, Haakon","Renaud, Paul E.","Smedsrud, Lars Henrik","Stige, Leif Christian","Arthun, Marius","Berge, Jørgen","Bluhm, Bodil A.","Borgå, Katrine","Bratbak, Gunnar","Divine, Dmitry V.","Eldevik, Tor","Eriksen, Elena","Fer, Ilker","Fransson, Agneta","Gradinger, Rolf","Granskog, Mats A.","Haug, Tore","Husum, Katrine","Johnsen, Geir","Jonassen, Marius O.","Jørgensen, Lis Lindal","Kristiansen, Svein","Larsen, Aud",