{"abstract":"Capacitive micromachined ultrasonic transducers (CMUTs) are inherently non-linear and often believed to be unsuitable for non-linear contrast-enhanced ultrasound (CEUS) imaging. The ability of CMUTs to perform contrast-enhanced ultrasound imaging has been investigated by experimentally evaluating the contrast-to-noise ratio (CTR) and its variation with emitted pressure. This has been evaluated using amplitude modulation, pulse inversion and B-mode imaging sequences. The study shows that the CTR of the AM-mode was 7.5 dB higher than the B-mode on average, while the PI-mode is 5.9 dB lower than the B-mode. This indicates that contrast-enhancement can be achieved with a CMUT when a suitable image sequence is chosen.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Ommen, Martin Lind","Engholm, Mathias","Schou, Mikkel","Diederichsen, Søren Elmin","Thomsen, Erik Vilain","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351321"],"event":{"end":"2020-09-11","place":"Las Vegas, us","start":"2020-09-06","title":"2020 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating a cmut s ability to achieve non linear contrast enhancement","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85097880352","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351321","identifier":[{"id":"85097880352","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9ccbacee-344b-4f2f-bad0-8c3c72297af8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-797B9037E7B3369B9B750AC69701F799"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigrid H.","key":"øygardpau","last":"Øygard","locid":"91316990-5af9-4a30-8cfc-d293dc4bd2e5","name":"Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","name_org":"Øygard, Sigrid H.","orcid":"0000-0002-3021-7812","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin L.","key":"ommenpau","last":"Ommen","locid":"e7aebb26-b70d-4857-8c80-0040af9b6102","name":"Ommen, Martin Lind","name_org":"Ommen, Martin L.","orcid":"0000-0001-9206-6426","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias","key":"engholmpau","last":"Engholm","locid":"d56e8d9d-6729-40bc-8782-91feda49b358","name":"Engholm, Mathias","orcid":"0000-0002-4277-2119","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"02abcc96-628c-467d-9117-1d3a80866a55","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren E.","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"bba32c4b-928b-44b9-9394-d0367a361ee6","name":"Diederichsen, Søren Elmin","name_org":"Diederichsen, Søren E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0686-913X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik V.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"822fe159-0932-4e5e-aeb6-b8b7f8421ab0","name":"Thomsen, Erik Vilain","name_org":"Thomsen, Erik V.","orcid":"0000-0002-2772-926X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ius46767.2020.9251326","eisbn":["9781728154480"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2020 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium (IUS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097880352"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9ccbacee-344b-4f2f-bad0-8c3c72297af8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Investigating a CMUT's Ability to Achieve Non-linear Contrast Enhancement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351321","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"A 3-D super resolution (SR) pipeline based on data from a Row-Column (RC) array is presented. The 3 MHz RC array contains 62 rows and 62 columns with a half wavelength pitch. A Synthetic Aperture (SA) pulse inversion sequence with 32 positive and 32 negative row emissions are used for acquiring volumetric data using the SARUS research ultrasound scanner. Data received on the 62 columns are beamformed on a GPU for a maximum volume rate of 156Hz, when the pulse repetition frequency is 10 kHz. Simulated and 3-D printed point and ﬂow micro-phantoms are used for investigating the approach. The ﬂow micro-phantom contains a 100 µm radius tube injected with the contrast agent SonoVue. The 3-D processing pipeline uses the volumetric envelope data to ﬁnd the bubble’s positions from their interpolated maximum signal and yields a high resolution in all three coordinates. For the point micro-phantom the standard deviation on the position is (20.7,19.8,9.1) µm (x,y,z). The precision estimated for the ﬂow phantom is below 23 µmin all three coordinates, making it possible to locate structures on the order of a capillary in all three dimensions. The RC imaging sequence’s point spread function has a size of 0.58 × 1.05 × 0.31 mm3 (1.17λ×2.12λ×0.63λ), so the possible volume resolution is 28,900 times smaller than for SA RC B-mode imaging.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Ommen, Martin Lind","Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Schou, Mikkel","Sams, Thomas","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Beers, Christopher","Thomsen, Erik Vilain","Larsen, Niels Bent","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324128"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three dimensional super resolution imaging using a row column array","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195822649/jensen_et_al_3D_SRI_with_RC_arrays_ver_4_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324128","identifier":[{"id":"85074176876","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31634831","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-41b3c815-d22d-4f1b-8402-c5c33f4c15f5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E12D6710E50C72B43005C0AE4158DA60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195822649/jensen_et_al_3D_SRI_with_RC_arrays_ver_4_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biomedical Engineering, Center for Fast Ultrasound Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["BK Medical ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e197c9fc-743f-4736-8d06-3825897e0989","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","orcid":"0000-0002-7896-3136","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Lind","key":"ommenpau","last":"Ommen","locid":"e7aebb26-b70d-4857-8c80-0040af9b6102","name":"Ommen, Martin Lind","orcid":"0000-0001-9206-6426","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigrid Husebø","key":"øygardpau","last":"Øygard","locid":"91316990-5af9-4a30-8cfc-d293dc4bd2e5","name":"Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","orcid":"0000-0002-3021-7812","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"02abcc96-628c-467d-9117-1d3a80866a55","name":"Schou, Mikkel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"samspau","last":"Sams","locid":"7237ce61-d883-44f0-b4a8-5c83749f6d51","name":"Sams, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-6316-2539","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Bo","key":"stuartpau","last":"Stuart","locid":"38dcc60f-13b3-4e3c-9561-93e13906ad24","name":"Stuart, Matthias Bo","orcid":"0000-0003-0809-530X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"beerspau","last":"Beers","name":"Beers, Christopher","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Vilain","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"822fe159-0932-4e5e-aeb6-b8b7f8421ab0","name":"Thomsen, Erik Vilain","orcid":"0000-0002-2772-926X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bent","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7a727b09-e209-47ab-80f7-9df731c2178f","name":"Larsen, Niels Bent","orcid":"0000-0001-6506-3991","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Borislav Gueorguiev","key":"tomovpau","last":"Tomov","locid":"16c6d791-3a1a-47ad-a725-2da30c420dee","name":"Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","orcid":"0000-0003-4236-3056","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31634831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tuffc.2019.2948563","issn":["08853010","15258955"],"issn_org":["08853010"],"issue":"3","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","pages":"538-546","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Ultrasonics, Ferroelectrics and Frequency Control","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074176876"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","bk medical aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-41b3c815-d22d-4f1b-8402-c5c33f4c15f5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Three-Dimensional Super Resolution Imaging using a Row-Column Array","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324128","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Ultrasound imaging of flow has seen a tremendous development over the last sixty years from 1-D spectral displays to color flow mapping and the latest Vector Flow Imaging (VFI). The paper gives an overview of the development from current commercial vector flow systems to the latest advances in fast 4-D volumetric visualizations. It includes a description of the radical break with the current sequential data acquisition by the introduction of synthetic aperture imaging, where the whole region of interest is insonified using either spherical or plane waves also known as ultrafast imaging. This makes it possible to track flow continuously in all directions at frame rates of thousands of images per second. The latest research translates this to full volumetric imaging by employing matrix arrays and row-column arrays for full 3-D vector velocity estimation at all spatial points visualized at very high volume rates (4-D).","author_count":32,"contributors":["Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","Nikolov, Svetoslav Ivanov","Hansen, Kristoffer Lindskov","Stuart, Matthias Bo","Hoyos, Carlos A. Villagomez","Schou, Mikkel","Ommen, Martin Lind","Øygard, Sigrid Husebø","Jørgensen, Lasse Thurmann","Traberg, Marie Sand","Nguyen, Tin-Quoc","Thomsen, Erik Vilain","Larsen, Niels Bent","Beers, Christopher","Tomov, Borislav Gueorguiev","Bachmann Nielsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-082.16-037667"],"event":{"end":"2019-10-09","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2019-10-06","title":"2019 IEEE International Ultrasonics Symposium, IUS 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":[